---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import credits from '../../assets/tamil-nadu/credits.json';
const plain=(html:string)=>html.replace(/<[^>]*>/g,' ').replace(/\s+/g,' ').trim();
---
<Base title="About & photo credits" description="Sources, photography credits and practical notes for Ula, an independent guide to temple towns, hill stations and coastal destinations."><section class="colophon wrap"><a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to Tamil Nadu</a><h1>A few field notes.</h1><h2>About Ula</h2><p>Ula is a personal portfolio concept for exploring tourist places in Tamil Nadu. It is not affiliated with the Government of Tamil Nadu or other Ula-branded services. The places are real; itineraries and durations are editorial suggestions, with no live availability or booking service.</p><h2>Destination information</h2><p>Destination background was checked against <a href="https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/tamil-nadu">Incredible India</a>, <a href="https://www.tamilnadutourism.tn.gov.in/">Tamil Nadu Tourism</a> and the <a href="https://chengalpattu.nic.in/tourist-place/mamallapuram/">Chengalpattu district guide to Mamallapuram</a>. Each destination page links to its official tourism source. Confirm opening hours and transport arrangements when planning your visit.</p><h2>Your trip brief</h2><p>The planner works in your browser. It saves a brief on this device when browser storage is available and lets you download a text file. It does not send your information or make a booking.</p><button class="text-link" id="clear-storage">Clear my saved trip brief</button><p id="storage-status" role="status"></p><h2>Photography credits</h2><p>Destination photographs are from Wikimedia Commons. Images have been resized, converted to WebP and AVIF and cropped by the layout. Each image retains its individual license; attribution and source links are below.</p><ul>{credits.map(c=><li><a href={c.source}>{c.slug.charAt(0).toUpperCase()+c.slug.slice(1)}</a> by {plain(c.author)} · <a href={c.licenseUrl||c.source}>{c.license}</a></li>)}</ul><h2>Typography & design</h2><p><a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/DM+Sans">DM Sans</a> is self-hosted under the SIL Open Font License. Built with Astro, GSAP and Lenis, guided by the <a href="https://github.com/juliobsz/skills/tree/main/awwwards">awwwards design skill</a>.</p></section></Base>
